From 922f4269e97394a1315dad171c69845fe31a627e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Serhii Nikolaichuk <nikolaichuk.s.f@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 09:36:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] sevsnp: the tests of our patches on real data, with AMD's KDS
 live

The revocation tests read AMD's CRLs from a snapshot of the KDS and
appraised at a fixed time inside its validity. They now fetch the CRLs
from the KDS with the scheme's own getter and check them at the time
they run, against the ASK and ARK the scheme trusts (amdRoots); without
the KDS they fail. The snapshot, the chains beside it and TestMain go.

- TestIntermediateNotRevoked: the Milan and Genoa ASKs are not revoked,
  and the CRL is fetched once per validity period. The Genoa ASK under a
  serial the Genoa CRL revokes is refused, and so are a CRL at its
  nextUpdate, another product line's CRL and a distribution point
  outside the KDS.
- TestForgedCRL refused a CRL the test made with a key of its own; it
  now refuses AMD's Milan CRL as the KDS serves it, with the last octet
  of its signature changed.
- TestIntegrityNeedsTheCRL stood the KDS in with a getter that returned
  an error; the getter now fetches over HTTPS as the scheme's does, with
  its connections sent to a local port nothing listens on, so the
  failure is the network's.
- TestTrustedIssuerUnknownLeaf made up a certificate; it now takes a
  real one that AMD did not issue, Google's root for its launch
  endorsements (test/certs/SOURCES.md).
- The DER certificate table was made by re-encoding the PEM table of
  upstream's report. The test now takes a report from a Google Cloud
  guest, with the table as the host supplied it, and the trust anchor of
  the attestation-bench CoRIM (test/evidence/SOURCES.md,
  test/corim/SOURCES.md).
- TestMatchSkipsMitigationVectors matched vectors the test made up; it
  now matches the claims of that Google Cloud report, which holds its
  vectors, against the reference values go-gen-ref makes from it and
  those of the attestation-bench CoRIM.
